💻 Personal Portfolio – Dumala Honey
📌 Objective

The objective of this project is to design and develop a personal portfolio website that showcases your professional profile, skills, and projects. The goal is to create an online presence that highlights your abilities as a Web Developer and Designer, allowing visitors and recruiters to easily explore your work and contact you.

🧩 Steps Performed
1.Project Setup
Created the main HTML structure using index.html.
Linked external stylesheets (style.css) and Font Awesome icons for better UI and branding.

2.Navigation Bar
Added a fixed navigation bar with links to Home, About Me, Projects, and Contact sections.
Included social media icons (Email, LinkedIn, GitHub) for quick connectivity.

3.Home Section
Displayed a personal introduction with name, title, and a professional photo.
Added quick-access links for contacting via email or visiting social profiles.

4.About Section
Included a short bio describing your passion for web development and design.
Highlighted your interest in building interactive and creative web applications.

5.Projects Section
Showcased sample projects with flip-card animations for interactivity.
Example projects include:
Simple Calculator – Built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
Dice Rolling Game – Fun and interactive JS-based game.
Tic Tac Toe – A browser-based classic game.
6.Contact Section
Added a contact form (connected to Formspree) allowing users to send messages directly.
Included footer with copyright, social icons, and a thank-you note.

🛠️ Tools & Technologies Used

HTML5 – Website structure and content layout.
CSS3 – Styling, animations, and responsive design.
Font Awesome – For professional icon integration.
Formspree – To handle form submissions easily.
Visual Studio Code – As the code editor.

🎯 Outcome

A fully responsive portfolio website that presents your professional identity and projects attractively.
Visitors can learn about your skills, view your projects, and contact you directly.
Clean UI design with smooth navigation, interactive elements, and a modern aesthetic.
